From: egui-aros
Subject: [PATCH] aros-gui-sys: text in the system character set; FTXT CSET

Repository: aros-development-team/AROS bf7075aab8480cf36bdc13b4382ccbd6098c8a0d,
  tools/crosstools/rust/crates/aros-gui-sys.
Date: 2026-11-07
Problem: the glue documented its text as ISO 8859-1, and the winit and
  egui-winit backends converted keys, titles and clipboard text that way. A
  Polish keymap types ISO 8859-2 ("ąę" are 0xB1 0xEA), so egui received
  "±ê"; Polish text pasted from other AROS programs was garbled the same way,
  and text written to the clipboard lost every character outside ISO 8859-1.
Rationale: AROS keeps the user's set in ENV:CHARSET (Locale preferences
  write a codesets.library name there); keymaps and other programs' FTXT
  CHRS use it, and AROS's own writers add no CSET chunk. TextEditor.mcc and
  BetterString.mcc read an FTXT CSET chunk whose first long is the IANA
  MIBenum, 106 being UTF-8. The glue now:
  - copies that set's byte -> UCS-4 table from codesets.library
    (aros_gui_charset_table), falling back to the library's default set and
    then to ISO 8859-1; UTF-8 as CHARSET is reported as such;
  - reads and writes FTXT with CSET (aros_gui_clip_read_cset/_write_cset);
    the old two functions remain, as cset 0.
  The crate root now builds on every target: `charset` (the codec and the
  system set) and `clipboard` (FTXT payload rules) are plain Rust with host
  tests; the raw bindings moved unchanged to `sys`, still AROS only.
  Writing: text the system set holds goes out in that set without CSET, so
  every AROS program reads it; other text goes out as UTF-8 with CSET 106
  instead of question marks.
Scope: no change to existing functions' behaviour; new functions only.
Upstream-status: candidate for the AROS crate store (not submitted).
Verification: host tests (9); C compiled with -Wall -Wextra
  -Werror=implicit-function-declaration for x86_64 ABIv11 (GCC 10.5), x86_64
  ABIv1 (GCC 10.5, nightly 20261105 SDK) and aarch64 (Clang); runtime: see the
  egui-aros records.
Removal: when the AROS crate store carries an equivalent change.
